\layout Subsubsection

Formulation discrete
\layout Standard

Comme indique, il est possible de garder la meme formulation en termes de
 flux pour la correction de premier ordre de l'equation de Fokker-Planck
 qui decrit les effets de derive.
 On conserve donc pour les expressions discretes les meme notations concernant
 les indices.
 La premiere quantite a calculer a partir de l'equation de Fokker-Planck
 d'ordre zero est la fonction 
\begin_inset Formula $\widetilde{f}^{(0)}$
\end_inset 


\begin_inset Formula \[
\widetilde{f}^{(0)}(p,\xi_{0},r)=-\frac{p\xi_{0}}{q_{e}B_{\theta,0}}\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}(p,\xi_{0},r)}{\partial r}\]

\end_inset 

 qui est non-nulle en presence d'un gradient de pression.
 La grille radiale pouvant etre non-uniforme, il convient de determiner
 precisement la derivee radiale.
\layout Standard

Soient 
\begin_inset Formula $r_{-},r$
\end_inset 

 et 
\begin_inset Formula $r_{+}$
\end_inset 

 les trois positions radiales ou sont calculees les ditributions 
\begin_inset Formula $f_{0}^{(0)}.$
\end_inset 

 Posons 
\begin_inset Formula $\Delta r_{-}=r_{-}-r,$
\end_inset 

 
\begin_inset Formula $\Delta r_{+}=r_{+}-r$
\end_inset 

 et 
\begin_inset Formula $\Delta r=r_{+}-r_{-}$
\end_inset 

.
 On considere une interpolation parabolique de la forme 
\begin_inset Formula $y=ar^{2}+br+c$
\end_inset 

 pour calculer la derivee radiale qui vaut 
\begin_inset Formula $\frac{dy}{dr}=2ar+b.$
\end_inset 

 Les coefficients 
\begin_inset Formula $a,b$
\end_inset 

 et 
\begin_inset Formula $c$
\end_inset 

 etant determines par les valeurs 
\begin_inset Formula $y_{-},y$
\end_inset 

 et 
\begin_inset Formula $y_{+}$
\end_inset 

 aux points 
\begin_inset Formula $r_{-},r$
\end_inset 

 et 
\begin_inset Formula $r_{+},$
\end_inset 

 on montre alors simplement que 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\left.\frac{dy}{dr}\right|_{r=r_{0}}=\frac{1}{\det V}\left(-\Delta r_{+}^{2}y_{-}+\Delta r\left(\Delta r_{+}+\Delta r_{-}\right)y_{0}+\Delta r_{-}^{2}y_{+}\right)\]

\end_inset 

 ou 
\begin_inset Formula $\overline{\overline{V}}$
\end_inset 

 est la matrice de Van der Monde d'ordre 3 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\overline{\overline{V}}=\left[\begin{array}{lll}
1 & r_{-} & r_{-}^{2}\\
1 & r & r^{2}\\
1 & r_{+} & r_{+}^{2}\end{array}\right]\]

\end_inset 

 dont le determinant vaut 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\det V=-\Delta r_{+}\Delta r_{-}\Delta r\]

\end_inset 


\layout Standard

On obtient alors 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\left.\frac{dy}{dr}\right|_{r}=\frac{\Delta r_{+}}{\Delta r\Delta r_{-}}y_{-}-\frac{\left(\Delta r_{+}+\Delta r_{-}\right)}{\Delta r_{+}\Delta r_{-}}y-\frac{\Delta r_{-}}{\Delta r\Delta r_{+}}y_{+}\]

\end_inset 

 et pour 
\begin_inset Formula $\widetilde{f}^{(0)},$
\end_inset 


\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
 &  & \widetilde{f}_{0}^{(0)(k+1)}(p_{i+1/2},\xi_{0,j+1/2},r_{l+1/2})=-\frac{p\xi_{0,j+1/2}}{q_{e}B_{\theta,0,l+1/2}}\times\\
 &  & \left[\frac{\left(r_{l+3/2}-r_{l+1/2}\right)}{\left(r_{l+3/2}-r_{l-1/2}\right)\left(r_{l-1/2}-r_{l+1/2}\right)}f_{0}^{(0)(k+1)}(p_{i+1/2},\xi_{0,j+1/2},r_{l-1/2})\right.\\
 &  & -\frac{\left(r_{l+3/2}-2r_{l+1/2}+r_{l-1/2}\right)}{\left(r_{l+3/2}-r_{l+1/2}\right)\left(r_{l-1/2}-r_{l+1/2}\right)}f_{0}^{(0)(k+1)}(p_{i+1/2},\xi_{0,j+1/2},r_{l+1/2})\\
 &  & -\left.\frac{\left(r_{l-1/2}-r_{l+1/2}\right)}{\left(r_{l+3/2}-r_{l-1/2}\right)\left(r_{l+3/2}-r_{l+1/2}\right)}f_{0}^{(0)(k+1)}(p_{i+1/2},\xi_{0,j+1/2},r_{l+3/2})\right]\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 


\layout Standard

Par ailleurs, il convient de reexprimer l'equation conservative faisant
 intervenir 
\begin_inset Formula $\widetilde{f}^{(0)}$
\end_inset 

 sous forme discrete, puisque des termes d'interpolation nouveaux vont apparaitr
e compte tenu des effets de gradients.
 D'apres la formulation conservative universelle 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\widetilde{\mathbf{S}}_{\mathbf{p}}^{(0)}=-\overline{\overline{\widetilde{D}}}^{(0)}\cdot\nabla_{p,\xi_{0}}\widetilde{f}^{(0)}+\overline{\widetilde{F}}^{(0)}\widetilde{f}^{(0)}\]

\end_inset 

 les valeurs suivantes de 
\begin_inset Formula $\widetilde{f}^{(0)}$
\end_inset 

 qui apparaissent sur la grille entiere en 
\begin_inset Formula $\left(p,\xi\right)$
\end_inset 

 a la position radiale 
\begin_inset Formula $l+1/2$
\end_inset 

 sont 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\left\{ \begin{array}{l}
\widetilde{f}_{i+1,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}=-\frac{p_{i+1}\xi_{0,j+1/2}}{q_{e}B_{\theta,0,l+1/2}}\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial r}\right|_{i+1,j+1/2}^{(k+1)}\\
\widetilde{f}_{i,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}=-\frac{p_{i}\xi_{0,j+1/2}}{q_{e}B_{\theta,0,l+1/2}}\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial r}\right|_{i,j+1/2}^{(k+1)}\\
\widetilde{f}_{i+1/2,j+1}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}=-\frac{p_{i+1/2}\xi_{0,j+1}}{q_{e}B_{\theta,0,l+1/2}}\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial r}\right|_{i+1/2,j+1}^{(k+1)}\\
\widetilde{f}_{i+1/2,j}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}=-\frac{p_{i+1/2}\xi_{0,j}}{q_{e}B_{\theta,0,l+1/2}}\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial r}\right|_{i+1/2,j}^{(k+1)}\end{array}\right.\]

\end_inset 


\layout Standard

En reportant les expressions des interpolations de la distribution 
\begin_inset Formula $f_{0}^{(0)}$
\end_inset 

 donnees au paragraphe precedent en 
\begin_inset Formula $l+1/2$
\end_inset 

, on obtient donc 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial r}\right|_{i+1,j+1/2}^{(k+1)} & = & \left(1-\delta_{p,i+1,j+1/2}^{(0)}\right)\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial r}\right|_{i+3/2,j+1/2}^{(k+1)}+\delta_{p,i+1,j+1/2}^{(0)}\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial r}\right|_{i+1/2,j+1/2}^{(k+1)}\\
 &  & -\frac{\partial\delta_{p,i+1,j+1/2}^{(0)}}{\partial r}\left[f_{0,i+3/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}-f_{0,i+1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}\right]\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 


\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial r}\right|_{i,j+1/2}^{(k+1)} & = & \left(1-\delta_{p,i,j+1/2}^{(0)}\right)\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial r}\right|_{i+1/2,j+1/2}^{(k+1)}+\delta_{p,i,j+1/2}^{(0)}\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial r}\right|_{i-1/2,j+1/2}^{(k+1)}\\
 &  & -\frac{\partial\delta_{p,i,j+1/2}^{(0)}}{\partial r}\left[f_{0,i+1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}-f_{0,i-1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}\right]\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 


\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial r}\right|_{i+1/2,j+1}^{(k+1)} & = & \left(1-\delta_{\xi,i+1/2,j+1}^{(0)}\right)\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial r}\right|_{i+1/2,j+3/2}^{(k+1)}+\delta_{\xi,i+1/2,j+1}^{(0)}\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial r}\right|_{i+1/2,j+1/2}^{(k+1)}\\
 &  & -\frac{\partial\delta_{\xi,i+1/2,j+1}^{(0)}}{\partial r}\left[f_{0,i+1/2,j+3/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}-f_{0,i+1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}\right]\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 


\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial r}\right|_{i+1/2,j}^{(k+1)} & = & \left(1-\delta_{\xi,i+1/2,j}^{(0)}\right)\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial r}\right|_{i+1/2,j+1/2}^{(k+1)}+\delta_{\xi,i+1/2,j}^{(0)}\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial r}\right|_{i+1/2,j-1/2}^{(k+1)}\\
 &  & -\frac{\partial\delta_{\xi,i+1/2,j}^{(0)}}{\partial r}\left[f_{0,i+1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}-f_{0,i+1/2,j-1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}\right]\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 


\layout Standard

En multipliant les derivees par le coefficient 
\begin_inset Formula $-\frac{p\xi_{0}}{q_{e}B_{\theta,0}}$
\end_inset 

 a la position discrete appropriee, on trouve au point de grille 
\begin_inset Formula $\left(i+1,j+1/2\right),$
\end_inset 


\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\widetilde{f}_{i+1,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)} & = & -\frac{p_{i+1}\xi_{0,j+1/2}}{q_{e}B_{\theta,0,l+1/2}}\times\left[\left(1-\delta_{p,i+1,j+1/2}^{(0)}\right)\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial r}\right|_{i+3/2,j+1/2}^{(k+1)}\right.\\
 &  & +\delta_{p,i+1,j+1/2}^{(0)}\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial r}\right|_{i+1/2,j+1/2}^{(k+1)}\\
 &  & -\frac{\partial\delta_{p,i+1,j+1/2}^{(0)}}{\partial r}f_{0,i+3/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}\\
 &  & \left.+\frac{\partial\delta_{p,i+1,j+1/2}^{(0)}}{\partial r}f_{0,i+1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}\right]\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 

 soit 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\widetilde{f}_{i+1,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)} & = & \left(1-\delta_{p,i+1,j+1/2}^{(0)}\right)\frac{p_{i+1}}{p_{i+3/2}}\widetilde{f}_{i+3/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}\\
 &  & +\delta_{p,i+1,j+1/2}^{(0)}\frac{p_{i+1}}{p_{i+1/2}}\widetilde{f}_{i+1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}\\
 &  & +\frac{p_{i+1}\xi_{0,j+1/2}}{q_{e}B_{\theta,0,l+1/2}}\frac{\partial\delta_{p,i+1,j+1/2}^{(0)}}{\partial r}f_{0,i+3/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}\\
 &  & -\frac{p_{i+1}\xi_{0,j+1/2}}{q_{e}B_{\theta,0,l+1/2}}\frac{\partial\delta_{p,i+1,j+1/2}^{(0)}}{\partial r}f_{0,i+1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 

 , au point de grille 
\begin_inset Formula $\left(i,j+1/2\right),$
\end_inset 


\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\widetilde{f}_{i,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)} & = & -\frac{p_{i}\xi_{0,j+1/2}}{q_{e}B_{\theta,0,l+1/2}}\times\left[\left(1-\delta_{p,i,j+1/2}^{(0)}\right)\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial r}\right|_{i+1/2,j+1/2}^{(k+1)}\right.\\
 &  & +\delta_{p,i,j+1/2}^{(0)}\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial r}\right|_{i-1/2,j+1/2}^{(k+1)}\\
 &  & -\frac{\partial\delta_{p,i,j+1/2}^{(0)}}{\partial r}f_{0,i+1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}\\
 &  & \left.+\frac{\partial\delta_{p,i,j+1/2}^{(0)}}{\partial r}f_{0,i-1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}\right]\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 

 soit 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\widetilde{f}_{i,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)} & = & \left(1-\delta_{p,i,j+1/2}^{(0)}\right)\frac{p_{i}}{p_{i+1/2}}\widetilde{f}_{i+1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}\\
 &  & +\delta_{p,i,j+1/2}^{(0)}\frac{p_{i}}{p_{i-1/2}}\widetilde{f}_{i-1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}\\
 &  & +\frac{p_{i}\xi_{0,j+1/2}}{q_{e}B_{\theta,0,l+1/2}}\frac{\partial\delta_{p,i,j+1/2}^{(0)}}{\partial r}f_{0,i+1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}\\
 &  & -\frac{p_{i}\xi_{0,j+1/2}}{q_{e}B_{\theta,0,l+1/2}}\frac{\partial\delta_{p,i,j+1/2}^{(0)}}{\partial r}f_{0,i-1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 

 , au point de grille 
\begin_inset Formula $\left(i+1/2,j+1\right),$
\end_inset 


\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\widetilde{f}_{i+1/2,j+1}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)} & = & -\frac{p_{i+1/2}\xi_{0,j+1}}{q_{e}B_{\theta,0,l+1/2}}\times\left[\left(1-\delta_{\xi,i+1/2,j+1}^{(0)}\right)\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial r}\right|_{i+1/2,j+3/2}^{(k+1)}\right.\\
 &  & +\delta_{\xi,i+1/2,j+1}^{(0)}\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial r}\right|_{i+1/2,j+1/2}^{(k+1)}\\
 &  & -\frac{\partial\delta_{\xi,i+1/2,j+1}^{(0)}}{\partial r}f_{0,i+1/2,j+3/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}\\
 &  & \left.+\frac{\partial\delta_{\xi,i+1/2,j+1}^{(0)}}{\partial r}f_{0,i+1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}\right]\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 

 soit 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\widetilde{f}_{i+1/2,j+1}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)} & = & \left(1-\delta_{\xi,i+1/2,j+1}^{(0)}\right)\frac{\xi_{0,j+1}}{\xi_{0,j+3/2}}\widetilde{f}_{i+1/2,j+3/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}\\
 &  & +\delta_{\xi,i+1/2,j+1}^{(0)}\frac{\xi_{0,j+1}}{\xi_{0,j+1/2}}\widetilde{f}_{i+1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}\\
 &  & +\frac{p_{i+1/2}\xi_{0,j+1}}{q_{e}B_{\theta,0,l+1/2}}\frac{\partial\delta_{\xi,i+1/2,j+1}^{(0)}}{\partial r}f_{0,i+1/2,j+3/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}\\
 &  & -\frac{p_{i+1/2}\xi_{0,j+1}}{q_{e}B_{\theta,0,l+1/2}}\frac{\partial\delta_{\xi,i+1/2,j+1}^{(0)}}{\partial r}f_{0,i+1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 

 et finalement en 
\begin_inset Formula $\left(i+1/2,j\right),$
\end_inset 


\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\widetilde{f}_{i+1/2,j}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)} & = & -\frac{p_{i+1/2}\xi_{0,j}}{q_{e}B_{\theta,0,l+1/2}}\times\left[\left(1-\delta_{\xi,i+1/2,j}^{(0)}\right)\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial r}\right|_{i+1/2,j+1/2}^{(k+1)}\right.\\
 &  & +\delta_{\xi,i+1/2,j}^{(0)}\left.\frac{\partial f_{0}^{(0)}}{\partial r}\right|_{i+1/2,j-1/2}^{(k+1)}\\
 &  & -\frac{\partial\delta_{\xi,i+1/2,j}^{(0)}}{\partial r}f_{0,i+1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}\\
 &  & \left.+\frac{\partial\delta_{\xi,i+1/2,j}^{(0)}}{\partial r}f_{0,i+1/2,j-1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}\right]\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 

 soit 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\widetilde{f}_{i+1/2,j}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)} & = & \left(1-\delta_{\xi,i+1/2,j}^{(0)}\right)\frac{\xi_{0,j}}{\xi_{0,j+3/2}}\widetilde{f}_{i+1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}\\
 &  & +\delta_{\xi,i+1/2,j}^{(0)}\frac{\xi_{0,j}}{\xi_{0,j+1/2}}\widetilde{f}_{i+1/2,j-1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}\\
 &  & +\frac{p_{i+1/2}\xi_{0,j}}{q_{e}B_{\theta,0,l+1/2}}\frac{\partial\delta_{\xi,i+1/2,j}^{(0)}}{\partial r}f_{0,i+1/2,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}\\
 &  & -\frac{p_{i+1/2}\xi_{0,j}}{q_{e}B_{\theta,0,l+1/2}}\frac{\partial\delta_{\xi,i+1/2,j}^{(0)}}{\partial r}f_{0,i+1/2,j-1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 


\layout Standard

Pour calculer les coefficients des matrices correspondant au terme source
 
\begin_inset Formula $\left\{ r\nabla\cdot\mathbf{S}_{\mathbf{p}}^{\widetilde{f}}\right\} $
\end_inset 

 pour l'equation de derive cinetique, il convient de reexprimer explicitement
 son expression 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\left\{ r\nabla\cdot\mathbf{S}_{\mathbf{p}}^{\widetilde{f}}\right\} _{i+1/2,j+1/2,l+1/2} & = & +r_{l+1/2}\frac{-p_{i+1}^{2}\widetilde{D}_{pp,i+1,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)}\left.\frac{\partial\widetilde{f}^{\left(0\right)}}{\partial p}\right|_{i+1,j+1/2}^{(k+1)}+p_{i+1}^{2}\widetilde{F}_{p,i+1,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)}\widetilde{f}_{i+1,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}}{\Delta p_{i+1/2}}\\
 &  & +r_{l+1/2}\frac{p_{i}^{2}\widetilde{D}_{pp,i,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)}\left.\frac{\partial\widetilde{f}^{\left(0\right)}}{\partial p}\right|_{i,j+1/2}^{(k+1)}-p_{i}^{2}\widetilde{F}_{p,i,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)}\widetilde{f}_{i,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}}{\Delta p_{i+1/2}}\\
 &  & +r_{l+1/2}\frac{p_{i+1}\widetilde{D}_{p\xi,i+1,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)}\sqrt{1-\xi_{0j+1/2}^{2}}\left.\frac{\partial\widetilde{f}^{\left(0\right)}}{\partial\left|\xi_{0}\right|}\right|_{i+1,j+1/2}^{(k+1)}-p_{i}\widetilde{D}_{p\xi,i,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)}\sqrt{1-\xi_{0j+1/2}^{2}}\left.\frac{\partial\widetilde{f}^{\left(0\right)}}{\partial\left|\xi_{0}\right|}\right|_{i,j+1/2}^{(k+1)}}{\Delta p_{i+1/2}}\\
 &  & -r_{l+1/2}\frac{\widetilde{D}_{\xi\xi,i+1/2,j+1}^{\left(0\right)}\left(1-\xi_{0j+1}^{2}\right)\left.\frac{\partial\widetilde{f}^{\left(0\right)}}{\partial\left|\xi_{0}\right|}\right|_{i+1/2,j+1}^{(k+1)}+p_{i+1/2}\sqrt{1-\xi_{0j+1}^{2}}\widetilde{F}_{\xi,i+1/2,j+1}^{\left(0\right)}\widetilde{f}_{i+1/2,j+1}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}}{\Delta\xi_{0j+1/2}}\frac{\lambda\left(\xi_{0j+1}\right)}{\lambda\left(\xi_{0j+1/2}\right)}\\
 &  & +r_{l+1/2}\frac{\widetilde{D}_{\xi\xi,i+1/2,j}^{\left(0\right)}\left(1-\xi_{0j}^{2}\right)\left.\frac{\partial\widetilde{f}^{\left(0\right)}}{\partial\left|\xi_{0}\right|}\right|_{i+1/2,j}^{(k+1)}+p_{i+1/2}\sqrt{1-\xi_{0j}^{2}}\widetilde{F}_{\xi,i+1/2,j}^{\left(0\right)}\widetilde{f}_{i+1/2,j}^{\left(0\right)(k+1)}}{\Delta\xi_{0j+1/2}}\frac{\lambda\left(\xi_{0j}\right)}{\lambda\left(\xi_{0j+1/2}\right)}\\
 &  & +r_{l+1/2}\frac{\lambda\left(\xi_{0j+1}\right)\sqrt{1-\xi_{0j+1}^{2}}p_{i+1/2}\widetilde{D}_{\xi p,i+1/2,j+1}^{\left(0\right)}\left.\frac{\partial\widetilde{f}^{\left(0\right)}}{\partial p}\right|_{i+1/2,j+1}^{(k+1)}-\lambda\left(\xi_{0j}\right)\sqrt{1-\xi_{0j}^{2}}p_{i+1/2}\widetilde{D}_{\xi p,i+1/2,j}^{\left(0\right)}\left.\frac{\partial\widetilde{f}^{\left(0\right)}}{\partial p}\right|_{i+1/2,j}^{(k+1)}}{\Delta\xi_{0j+1/2}\lambda\left(\xi_{0j+1/2}\right)}\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 


\layout Standard

On voit ainsi clairement que seuls les termes convectifs sont differents
 par rapport a l'expression 
\begin_inset Formula $\left\{ r\nabla\cdot\mathbf{S}_{\mathbf{p}}\right\} _{i+1/2,j+1/2,l+1/2}$
\end_inset 

 correspondant a l'equation de flux pour 
\begin_inset Formula $f_{0}^{\left(0\right)}.$
\end_inset 

 En reportant les expressions des termes d'interpolation entre les grilles
 entieres et demi-entieres, on obtient
\layout Standard


\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\left\{ r\nabla\cdot\mathbf{S}_{\mathbf{p}}^{\widetilde{f}}\right\} _{i+1/2,j+1/2,l+1/2} & = & -r_{l+1/2}\frac{p_{i+1}^{2}\widetilde{D}_{pp,i+1,j+1/2}^{\left(0\right)}\left.\frac{\partial\widetilde{f}^{\left(0\right)}}{\partial p}\right|_{i+1,j+1/2}^{(k+1)}}{\Delta p_{i+1/2}}\\
